From 0a549c2cf190e57c857f9a55b9b9b98ad17c5efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:22:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: label the concat-transpose prior-art numbers as
 upstream-reported, not ours

The comment above ggml_vk_concat_is_transposed carried "+45% pp2048 on a delta-net MoE, +3.3%
on a dense hybrid, never measured negative" as a bare assertion. Those are the PRIOR ART figures,
measured on gfx1151, and ArifiLabs has neither reproduced nor contradicted them. The commit message
and the git note both say so; the code - the artifact a reader of the published fork actually opens
- did not.

Independent check r2 raised it as a publication defect ahead of the fork going public. The comment
now separates the two claims by name: what upstream reported, and what we measured on a Radeon 780M
(the CONCAT dispatch 11-13% faster, about -13 to -16 ms per ub512 prefill graph, end-to-end ceiling
+0.18%, whole-model prefill a statistical TIE across two counterbalanced takes). Both truths stand
together: the op-level gain is real and the serve-level tie is not a loss.

Comment text only. No statement, no expression and no preprocessor directive changed, so the
canonical binaries built at 5b1b416cb remain valid for every gate result recorded against them.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Lane: lane-209
Measured-effect: none - comment text only, no generated code differs.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index a4b47bb1a6..591fb8e640 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -338,8 +338,19 @@ bool ggml_vk_concat_supported(const ggml_tensor * src0, const ggml_tensor * src1
 // is 160 * 256 B with 160 % 16 == 0, so every read lands on the same one of the 16 memory channels.
 // Route that exact shape to a tiled-transpose kernel instead.
 static bool ggml_vk_concat_is_transposed(const ggml_tensor * src0, const ggml_tensor * src1, const ggml_tensor * dst) {
-    // On by default: +45% pp2048 on a delta-net MoE, +3.3% on a dense hybrid, never measured
-    // negative. GGML_VK_CONCAT_TRANSPOSE=0 opts out.
+    // On by default. GGML_VK_CONCAT_TRANSPOSE=0 opts out.
+    //
+    // UPSTREAM-REPORTED, NOT REPRODUCED HERE: the prior art this kernel is ported from reports
+    // +45% pp2048 on a delta-net MoE, +3.3% on a dense hybrid, and never measured negative, on
+    // gfx1151. ArifiLabs has neither reproduced nor contradicted those figures.
+    //
+    // MEASURED BY ArifiLabs, on a Radeon 780M (gfx1103), Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL: the
+    // CONCAT dispatch itself is 11-13% faster, which is about -13 to -16 ms per ub512 prefill
+    // graph. CONCAT is ~1.4% of that graph, so the end-to-end ceiling is +0.18% and the
+    // whole-model prefill A/B is a statistical TIE on this device - measured twice,
+    // counterbalanced. The op-level gain is real and the serve-level tie is not a loss; both are
+    // true at once. Evidence: lane-209 rank 3, and `git notes show` on the commit that added
+    // this function.
     static const char * env = getenv("GGML_VK_CONCAT_TRANSPOSE");
     if (env && env[0] == '0') {
         return false;
